WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.333
John, Chapter Eight.

2
00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:03.600
Jesus went unto the mount of Olives.

3
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:10.933
And early in the morning he came again into the temple, and all the people came unto him; and he sat down, and taught them.

4
00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:21.867
And the scribes and Pharisees brought unto him a woman taken in adultery; and when they had set her in the midst, They say unto him, Master, this woman was taken in adultery, in the very act.

5
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:27.733
Now Moses in the law commanded us, that such should be stoned: but what sayest thou?

6
00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:31.333
This they said, tempting him, that they might have to accuse him.

7
00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:37.067
But Jesus stooped down, and with his finger wrote on the ground, as though he heard them not.

8
00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:45.200
So when they continued asking him, he lifted up himself, and said unto them, He that is without sin among you, let him first cast a stone at her.

9
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.133
And again he stooped down, and wrote on the ground.

10
00:00:48.133 --> 00:01:00.800
And they which heard it, being convicted by their own conscience, went out one by one, beginning at the eldest, even unto the last: and Jesus was left alone, and the woman standing in the midst.

11
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:08.933
When Jesus had lifted up himself, and saw none but the woman, he said unto her, Woman, where are those thine accusers?

12
00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:10.800
hath no man condemned thee?

13
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.800
She said, No man, Lord.

14
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:18.533
And Jesus said unto her, Neither do I condemn thee: go, and sin no more.

15
00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:27.467
Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.

16
00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:33.867
The Pharisees therefore said unto him, Thou bearest record of thyself; thy record is not true.

17
00:01:33.867 --> 00:01:45.200
Jesus answered and said unto them, Though I bear record of myself, yet my record is true: for I know whence I came, and whither I go; but ye cannot tell whence I come, and whither I go.

18
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.800
Ye judge after the flesh; I judge no man.

19
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:54.933
And yet if I judge, my judgment is true: for I am not alone, but I and the Father that sent me.

20
00:01:54.933 --> 00:01:59.067
It is also written in your law, that the testimony of two men is true.

21
00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:04.000
I am one that bear witness of myself, and the Father that sent me beareth witness of me.

22
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.200
Then said they unto him, Where is thy Father?

23
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:14.800
Jesus answered, Ye neither know me, nor my Father: if ye had known me, ye should have known my Father also.

24
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:23.200
These words spake Jesus in the treasury, as he taught in the temple: and no man laid hands on him; for his hour was not yet come.

25
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:32.000
Then said Jesus again unto them, I go my way, and ye shall seek me, and shall die in your sins: whither I go, ye cannot come.

26
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.800
Then said the Jews, Will he kill himself?

27
00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.533
because he saith, Whither I go, ye cannot come.

28
00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:46.133
And he said unto them, Ye are from beneath; I am from above: ye are of this world; I am not of this world.

29
00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:53.867
I said therefore unto you, that ye shall die in your sins: for if ye believe not that I am he, ye shall die in your sins.

30
00:02:53.867 --> 00:02:56.667
Then said they unto him, Who art thou?

31
00:02:56.667 --> 00:03:01.600
And Jesus saith unto them, Even the same that I said unto you from the beginning.

32
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:09.733
I have many things to say and to judge of you: but he that sent me is true; and I speak to the world those things which I have heard of him.

33
00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:12.667
They understood not that he spake to them of the Father.

34
00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:23.867
Then said Jesus unto them, When ye have lifted up the Son of man, then shall ye know that I am he, and that I do nothing of myself; but as my Father hath taught me, I speak these things.

35
00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:30.933
And he that sent me is with me: the Father hath not left me alone; for I do always those things that please him.

36
00:03:30.933 --> 00:03:33.867
As he spake these words, many believed on him.

37
00:03:33.867 --> 00:03:45.333
Then said Jesus to those Jews which believed on him, If ye continue in my word, then are ye my disciples indeed; And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.

38
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:54.133
They answered him, We be Abraham's seed, and were never in bondage to any man: how sayest thou, Ye shall be made free?

39
00:03:54.133 --> 00:04:00.133
Jesus answered them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Whosoever committeth sin is the servant of sin.

40
00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:05.600
And the servant abideth not in the house for ever: but the Son abideth ever.

41
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.867
If the Son therefore shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed.

42
00:04:09.867 --> 00:04:16.533
I know that ye are Abraham's seed; but ye seek to kill me, because my word hath no place in you.

43
00:04:16.533 --> 00:04:22.933
I speak that which I have seen with my Father: and ye do that which ye have seen with your father.

44
00:04:22.933 --> 00:04:26.267
They answered and said unto him, Abraham is our father.

45
00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:30.933
Jesus saith unto them, If ye were Abraham's children, ye would do the works of Abraham.

46
00:04:30.933 --> 00:04:38.133
But now ye seek to kill me, a man that hath told you the truth, which I have heard of God: this did not Abraham.

47
00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:40.267
Ye do the deeds of your father.

48
00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:46.800
Then said they to him, We be not born of fornication; we have one Father, even God.

49
00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:57.067
Jesus said unto them, If God were your Father, ye would love me: for I proceeded forth and came from God; neither came I of myself, but he sent me.

50
00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:59.467
Why do ye not understand my speech?

51
00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:04.000
even because ye cannot hear my word.

52
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.400
Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do.

53
00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:14.000
He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him.

54
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.933
When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.

55
00:05:18.933 --> 00:05:22.667
And because I tell you the truth, ye believe me not.

56
00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:24.667
Which of you convinceth me of sin?

57
00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:27.333
And if I say the truth, why do ye not believe me?

58
00:05:27.333 --> 00:05:34.400
He that is of God heareth God's words: ye therefore hear them not, because ye are not of God.

59
00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:41.200
Then answered the Jews, and said unto him, Say we not well that thou art a Samaritan, and hast a devil?

60
00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:46.933
Jesus answered, I have not a devil; but I honour my Father, and ye do dishonour me.

61
00:05:46.933 --> 00:05:51.467
And I seek not mine own glory: there is one that seeketh and judgeth.

62
00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:56.933
Verily, verily, I say unto you, If a man keep my saying, he shall never see death.

63
00:05:56.933 --> 00:06:01.200
Then said the Jews unto him, Now we know that thou hast a devil.

64
00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:08.667
Abraham is dead, and the prophets; and thou sayest, If a man keep my saying, he shall never taste of death.

65
00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:11.733
Art thou greater than our father Abraham, which is dead?

66
00:06:11.733 --> 00:06:15.333
and the prophets are dead: whom makest thou thyself?

67
00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:33.733
Jesus answered, If I honour myself, my honour is nothing: it is my Father that honoureth me; of whom ye say, that he is your God: Yet ye have not known him; but I know him: and if I should say, I know him not, I shall be a liar like unto you: but I know him, and keep his saying.

68
00:06:33.733 --> 00:06:39.200
Your father Abraham rejoiced to see my day: and he saw it, and was glad.

69
00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:45.733
Then said the Jews unto him, Thou art not yet fifty years old, and hast thou seen Abraham?

70
00:06:45.733 --> 00:06:51.867
Jesus said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Before Abraham was, I am.

71
00:06:51.867 --> 00:07:00.800
Then took they up stones to cast at him: but Jesus hid himself, and went out of the temple, going through the midst of them, and so passed by.

